.TH SQ 1 1.4.0 "Sequoia PGP" "User Commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
sq\-network\-keyserver\-publish \- Publish certificates on key servers
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.br
\fBsq network keyserver publish\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]  
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Publish certificates on key servers.
.PP
Sends certificates to the configured key servers for publication.  By default, the certificates are sent to `hkps://keys.openpgp.org`, `hkps://mail\-api.proton.me`, `hkps://keys.mailvelope.com`, `hkps://keyserver.ubuntu.com`, and `hkps://sks.pod01.fleetstreetops.com`.  This can be tweaked using `\-\-servers`.
.PP


.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.SS "Subcommand options"
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\fR=\fIFINGERPRINT|KEYID\fR
Use certificates with the specified fingerprint or key ID
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-domain\fR=\fIDOMAIN\fR
Use certificates where a user ID includes an email address for the specified domain
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-email\fR=\fIEMAIL\fR
Use certificates where a user ID includes the specified email address
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-file\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Read certificates from PATH
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\-userid\fR=\fIUSERID\fR
Use certificates with the specified user ID
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR=\fIURI\fR
Set a key server to use (can be given multiple times)
.IP
The default can be changed in the configuration file using the setting `network.keyserver.servers`.
.IP
[default: \fBhkps://keys.openpgp.org\fR, \fBhkps://mail\-api.proton.me\fR, \fBhkps://keys.mailvelope.com\fR, \fBhkps://keyserver.ubuntu.com\fR, \fBhkps://sks.pod01.fleetstreetops.com\fR]
.SS "Global options"
See \fBsq\fR(1) for a description of the global options.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.PP

.PP
Publish Alice's certificate on the default keyservers.
.PP
.nf
.RS
sq network keyserver publish \-\-cert\-email=alice@example.org
.RE
.fi
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.nh
\fBsq\fR(1), \fBsq\-network\fR(1), \fBsq\-network\-keyserver\fR(1).
.hy
.PP
For the full documentation see <https://book.sequoia\-pgp.org>.
.SH "نسخه (VERSION)"
1.4.0
